WEBVTT

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:08.993
This is Nexial. You pick a sector, and every morning you get the companies in it ranked by signal strength.

00:00:09.694 --> 00:00:16.310
Each row is a marker: a pattern across independent sources, never a single news item.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:22.090
On the right, the risk radar and the clusters forming in your sector.

00:00:22.791 --> 00:00:32.407
Open a company. You see the marker, its score, and a confidence level: confirmed, emerging, or hypothesis.

00:00:33.109 --> 00:00:43.901
Under it, the evidence: what was observed, when, and from which source. At least two independent sources, or the marker does not fire.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:49.009
A twelve-month timeline shows how the signals built up.

00:00:52.781 --> 00:01:00.693
Zoom out to the sector: where to look first, early warnings, and white spaces where capital has not arrived yet.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:07.914
Clusters are scored by signal convergence, so you see sub-segments forming before they have a name.

00:01:10.756 --> 00:01:17.036
And the investors: who is active, their deal pace, and who they co-invest with.

00:01:17.737 --> 00:01:23.873
Pick your sector. Fourteen-day free trial, no card required.
